1
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,500
Rise and shine!

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,420
Welcome to Mori-O-Radio.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,040
As usual, this is your host, Kai Harada,

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,537
keeping you company on this fine morning,

5
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,561
and I've got just the song
to start you off right.

6
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:36,760
Now, let's dig in, shall we?

7
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:40,811
Oh, but before we begin, I have
a little something for you.

8
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,960
Thank you.

9
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,677
What can I just share with you?

10
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,177
What can I do with myself?

11
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,037
What can I do with you?

12
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:36,950
It's a huge dream.

13
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:39,077
I know it's a giant bolt.

14
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:41,720
I know it's a giant bolt.

15
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:46,857
It's a giant bolt.

16
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:47,917
It's a giant

17
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:55,000
bolt.

18
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,462
I'll chase you!

19
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,817
I'll chase you tomorrow!

20
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,537
I'll do it again!

21
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:03,973
I'll change the future!

22
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:05,760
I'll change the future!

23
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:10,960
So I'll chase you!

24
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:29,317
For last minute but would you be
interested in getting lunch with us?

25
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,800
Apologies but I must decline.

26
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:36,897
I need to finish delivering these
documents before the day gets away from me.

27
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:38,500
Enjoy your lunch!

28
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,517
Don't waste your time on
him he'd suck the life

29
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,357
out of the party the guys
and I invite him out.

30
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:50,577
On occasion but we can never tell
if he's having fun or hates us?

31
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:54,400
Yoshikage Kira age 33. Every single.

32
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:57,237
He's a model employee,
that's for damn sure.

33
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:59,202
But the guy's dull as dishwater.

34
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:02,037
It's not that he's necessarily
a tool or anything.

35
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,240
He's just kind of blah, you know?

36
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:12,637
Oh, is that right?

37
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,477
Someone's a little bent out of shape.

38
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,817
Some new girls at work
invited me to lunch.

39
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,377
Really, it's as innocent as that.

40
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:21,480
But I promised you lunch
was our time together.

41
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:25,572
I'd never go back in my word
just to fraternize with them.

42
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:28,533
You heard me turn them down, didn't you?

43
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:33,257
In the time we've known each other,
I've never left you by your lonesome.

44
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:34,170
Right?

45
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,840
Good, it's settled.

46
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:40,517
Now stop this silly fretting and
let's pick out some sandwiches.

47
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,188
Now, which one do you want?

48
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,902
This one has a delicate texture.

49
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,857
This bakery's one of my favorites.

50
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:50,058
It makes sandwiches with
bread made fresh at 11 a .m.

51
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,837
They're all the rage around here.

52
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:55,038
You'd be lucky to find one
on the shelf after 1 p .m.

53
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,477
Even through the wrapper, you can
feel they're fresh from the oven.

54
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:02,325
The katsu they use is always
freshly fried and perfectly crispy.

55
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,360
What have we here?

56
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:10,346
It seems in all the excitement, you managed
to tear the wrapper and make a mess.

57
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:12,060
Such a naughty girl.

58
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:30,700
It's a waste, but this
sandwich is ruined now.

59
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:33,548
I suppose we'll just
buy the one underneath.

60
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:35,669
Thank you for dropping by.

61
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,037
Simply beautiful, isn't it?

62
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:57,417
Quaint little Mario between us, it might
be the most marvelous town on earth!

63
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:00,217
It's like we're on a romantic picnic,

64
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:07,300
a

65
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:14,700
bit

66
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,220
aromatic for? my taste.

67
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:19,362
I think it's time for the
two of us to part ways.

68
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:20,818
The end is close at

69
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,530
hand.

70
00:05:23,613 --> 00:05:24,443
Close at hand.

71
00:05:24,526 --> 00:05:25,700
If luck is on my side,

72
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:30,409
perhaps I'll cross paths with a beautiful
new girl visiting from out of town.

73
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,700
Oh joy, it's a mutt.

74
00:05:58,880 --> 00:05:59,710
Oh Huh?

75
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,950
Shigechi!

76
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:02,850
Hey!

77
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:07,380
Josuke and Okuyasu, good
to see you! What's up?

78
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,257
You know, you got here
just in the nick of time.

79
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:11,817
I'll get right to the point, okay?

80
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,557
We need to borrow some lunch money.

81
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:16,117
We're a little strapped
for cash at the moment.

82
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,030
Huh?

83
00:06:17,113 --> 00:06:18,431
How's that even possible?

84
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,857
What happened to the money we
got from the lottery ticket?

85
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:22,058
Is it gone already?

86
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,460
Don't be silly.

87
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,997
We put all that in the bank.

88
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,057
And you gotta be crazy
if you think we go all

89
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:29,217
the way to the bank just
to get some munch money.

90
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:30,577
It's not worth the walk.

91
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:32,857
A thousand yen should be
enough for both of us.

92
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:33,770
I agree.

93
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:37,797
Come on, as soon as school's over,
we'll head to the bank and pay you back.

94
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,320
Hey, I know that logo.

95
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:41,177
You got a sandwich from St.

96
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:42,090
Gentleman, didn't you?

97
00:06:42,173 --> 00:06:43,540
Well, what do you know?

98
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,637
I thought they were sold out.

99
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:48,277
They are, and you're not getting a
single bite of mine, you got that?

100
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,697
If you leave my sandwich alone,
I'll lend you guys the money.

101
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:54,074
Sweet, I can taste their lunch already.

102
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:56,290
Thank you.

103
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,917
And just so you know,
I'm writing an I .O .U.

104
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,177
for this little loan.

105
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:02,337
You're not gonna weasel out of this one.

106
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:03,250
Me?

107
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:05,159
You're the biggest weasel there is.

108
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:10,117
Okay, June 24th, lend
1,000 yen to needy friends.

109
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:12,260
Hang on. Lent.

110
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,597
How do you write the
character for Lent again?

111
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,510
Oh, well.

112
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:16,995
This'll work for now.

113
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,174
I guess Hiragana's better than nothing.

114
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,360
Crud, monkeys.

115
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:24,217
I don't know how to write
Josuke or Okuyasu either.

116
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,600
Huh? What the?

117
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,497
My sandwich was right there.

118
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:28,521
Where did it go?

119
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,480
What a relief.

120
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,580
My sandwich is safe and sound.

121
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:41,978
I don't remember it being this far
away, Hey, but at least I found it.

122
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,117
Th-that's...

123
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:56,020
Hey Josuke Okuyasu, wait up!

124
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:57,380
We're not done yet!

125
00:07:57,620 --> 00:08:01,091
I need your thumb prints on my
I .O .U to make it official!

126
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:07,057
You have got to be kidding me.

127
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:10,180
That lump of a brat
grabbed my back by mistake.

128
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:13,317
Come on, could you be any more annoying?

129
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,317
How would we give you our thumbprints?

130
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,230
It's simple.

131
00:08:16,313 --> 00:08:18,397
You cut your thumb with a
knife and use the blood.

132
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,517
What are you talking about?

133
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,177
We don't have to go that far.

134
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:23,672
Just sign the IOU and we'll call it good.

135
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,837
Yeah, yeah, but let's haul ass to St.

136
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,744
Gentleman before they sell out.

137
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:28,690
Damn it.

138
00:08:28,773 --> 00:08:30,914
I can't let him see what's in that bag.

139
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:34,957
She's still wearing the ring I
put on her finger this morning.

140
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,820
It has my fingerprints on it.

141
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:39,297
So when the police open an investigation,

142
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:43,086
it'll be just a matter of time
before they trace it back to me.

143
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:49,167
Yoshikage Kira has been
at this for 15 years,

144
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:52,419
and in all that time, he's
never left a single clue.

145
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:55,053
This pathetic whelp isn't changing that.

146
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:57,520
Hey, Josuke, let's head in. Right.

147
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:01,013
I'll stay outside and wait for you guys.

148
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:05,020
My best bet is to take it by force.

149
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:09,689
On second thought, I'd better
snatch it without his knowing.

150
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:15,410
Shigechi!

151
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:17,957
You're a lucky son of
a gun, you know that?

152
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:21,017
The lunchtime rush beat us here
and they're already out of St.

153
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,177
Gentleman's sandwiches.

154
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:23,100
Just our luck.

155
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,237
They're sold out, huh?

156
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,791
Well, isn't that a shame?

157
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:28,420
I feel bad for you guys, I really do.

158
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:33,347
I guess I could sell you mine, but so
you know it'll cost you 10,000 yen, okay?

159
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,460
Boy, not a decent bone
in your body, is there?

160
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:41,737
All right, Josuke, looks
like we're headed to Hokuben.

161
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,297
You sure that'll be enough?

162
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:46,520
I doubt a 500 yen meal and
a drink will fill us up.

163
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:47,917
We're better off skipping it.

164
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,497
It's not my first choice, but
the cafeteria will do just fine.

165
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:54,137
Besides, that's where Koichi
said he's getting lunch today.

166
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:57,477
Oh man, that means he'll be
there with Yukako Yamagishi.

167
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:01,619
I hate having to be the third wheel
to those honeymooners' love fest.

168
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:03,897
And the food they serve is terrible.

169
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:07,117
Their nasty meat is so thin,
it's practically invisible.

170
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,277
And who knows what kind of weird
shit they put in the Masa soup.

171
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:13,297
Hey, why don't we use the equipment
room in my middle school's gym?

172
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:15,437
It has tons of drinks to choose from.

173
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,717
Our PE teacher always
sneaks away to have his

174
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,917
coffee and tea in there
when no one's looking.

175
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,277
All the teachers are in the
faculty room during lunch,

176
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,057
so they won't be able to bust us.

177
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:27,917
Sometimes I'll sneak in through the
window and take a cup to quench my thirst.

178
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,757
Why don't you go buy lunch and we'll
hang out there and eat together?

179
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,217
Let's back it up there, Shigechi.

180
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,637
Are you seriously stealing
drinks from school?

181
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,080
You stingy bastard!

182
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,297
Can't you even buy drinks for yourself?

183
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,877
You've never seen me doing
something that greedy.

184
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,880
See you later.

185
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,637
Geez, what crawled up there butts?

186
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:46,426
I was just trying to be nice.

187
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:50,420
Okay, well, you better pay me
back my thousand yen tomorrow.

188
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:07,277
Sorry for bumping into you sir it's all my
fault I wasn't looking where I was going.

189
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:12,837
Sorry again shit so close he's left his

190
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:14,457
idiotic friends but he's heading back to

191
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:18,177
school he's eating
lunch there so what's my

192
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:22,677
next move I believe
they call him Shigechi.

193
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:26,540
Minutes from now he'll open that
bag and things will get very

194
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:28,310
complicated.

195
00:11:28,393 --> 00:11:30,540
Damn it, this is unfathomable.

196
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,070
Alrighty,

197
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:51,691
now that I'm in my special hiding spot,
I can finally eat my lunch in peace.

198
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:00,610
Oh, yeah!

199
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:02,432
How did I almost forget?

200
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:05,997
Before I start chowing down on
my food, I need to make coffee.

201
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:09,786
It's not a secret trip to the
gym without a freshly brewed cup.

202
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,900
Fortune has smiled on you, Shigechi.

203
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:22,793
Had you peeked inside, my only recourse
would have been to obliterate you.

204
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:31,180
Josuke, I think this is the place.

205
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,140
It's smaller than I thought. What the?

206
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:36,500
Why are they here?

207
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:39,191
I thought these two were blowing them off.

208
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,110
Shigechi!

209
00:12:43,193 --> 00:12:44,057
You here or what?

210
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,280
Shigechi! Huh?

211
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,397
Hey, what are you doing here?

212
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,577
I thought you were going to
get lunch somewhere else.

213
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,719
That was the plan.

214
00:12:50,820 --> 00:12:53,457
We couldn't just pass up
free coffee from Cafe Gym.

215
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:56,740
We got 500 yen Mega
nochi bentos on the way!

216
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,010
Wow!

217
00:12:59,093 --> 00:13:03,137
I can't believe you two actually showed up
to eat after calling me a stingy bastard.

218
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:05,197
You're a couple of hypocritical pricks.

219
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:07,162
Come on, man, cut us some slack.

220
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:09,297
Haven't you heard of people
changing their minds?

221
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:11,556
It is a thing that happens, you know.

222
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:15,397
Now what do I do?

223
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,437
Offing one of them would
be a walk in the park,

224
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,696
but I can't tackle all three at once.

225
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:22,100
Shit, I was so close, too.

226
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:24,227
She's only centimeters away.

227
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:31,357
Shigechi, you mind grabbing
me a drink on your way back?

228
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:33,797
And could you make it a
green tea instead of coffee?

229
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:36,440
I'll take a black tea with milk. Really?

230
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,612
Makunochi with milk tea?

231
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,073
That sounds disgusting.

232
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:44,337
Shit, he's going to try to eat his
meal right on top of this thing.

233
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:49,126
If I don't do something fast, he's going
to open the bag right in front of them.

234
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:59,700
Ah, not soy sauce again.

235
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:03,480
They're always giving me
soy sauce with katsu. Huh?

236
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:05,357
That's how you're supposed to eat it.

237
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,220
No way. Don't be stupid.

238
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,397
Everyone knows it's tonkatsu sauce.

239
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:12,715
Putting soy sauce on tonkatsu
violates all that sacred.

240
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,781
Like it matters.

241
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,430
Yes.

242
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,430
Damn it.

243
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,430
What the hell?

244
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:49,240
Damn it.

245
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,160
What the hell?

246
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,940
Just a minute!

247
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,614
What exactly do you think you're doing?

248
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,550
Talk!

249
00:15:05,633 --> 00:15:06,777
Because from where I'm standing,

250
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:09,437
it looks like you're trying to
steal my sandwich out from under me!

251
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,350
As if.

252
00:15:10,433 --> 00:15:11,871
Stop being such an idiot.

253
